    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d200">

                <pb facs="0348" n="1812" sameAs="frus:frus1951v06p2/pg1812"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">690D.91/8–151: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Embassy in Pakistan
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-08-10T16:00:00-04:00">August 10, 1951—4
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>157. Dept doubts feasibility Graham making informal interim report mid-Aug (last
                    para Embtel 114, Aug 1) because 1) his
                    obvious unwillingness devote himself to present crisis (Delhi tel 321 rptd Kar
                    21, Aug [<hi rendition="#italic">July</hi>] 23) 2) such report not essential to
                    permit SC action if necessary and 3) it wld
                    undoubtedly prejudice successful conclusion Graham present work by possibly
                    prematurely showing his hand.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
